/*  Sets — `a set of text with (…)`, `has`, inserting, `the number of`, and looping over one.

    ★ A set is the map it is stored as: each element its own key AND its own value, as in
      `cufet build`. So membership asks the key, inserting what is already there changes nothing,
      looping hands back the values in the order they went in — and a set prints as that map, as the
      interpreter prints it.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to is-set, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "set of ".
    Done.

    /// What a set holds.
    Bind text to set-element, given (the text kind):
        Return the characters from 8 to the end of kind.
    Done.

    /// The map a set is stored as.
    Bind text to set-storage, given (the text kind):
        Define element as cast set-element on (kind).
        Return "map from {element} to {element}".
    Done.

    /// The kind of a set of `element`, its map noted for writing — or a failure for an element no
    /// map can be keyed by yet.
    Bind text or failure to set-kind-of-element unto emitter, given (the text element):
        If cast is-scalar on (element) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a set of {element}")).
        Cast one's map-kind-of-type on (element, element) or pass the failure off.
        Return "set of {element}".
    Done.

    /// The kind of a set expression.
    Bind text or failure to set-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        If expression's kind is "SetHasMember", return "fact".
        Define element as "void".
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) is false:
            The element becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if the number of (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s children is greater than 0:
            The element becomes cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s children) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast one's set-kind-of-element on (element) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// A set expression as C: a literal, its elements put in order, or a membership test.
    Bind text or failure to c-set-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        If expression's kind is "SetHasMember":
            Define set-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define set-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define member-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), cast set-element on (set-kind)) or pass the failure off.
            Define sides as a series of text with (set-c, member-c).
            Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2)), sides).
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, "{cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (set-kind))}_has({item 1 of sides}, {item 2 of sides})").
        Done.
        Define set-kind as cast one's set-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (set-kind)).
        Define built as "(\{ {map-c}* cf_set = {map-c}_new();".
        For each written in (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define element-c as cast one's c-of-as on (written, cast set-element on (set-kind)) or pass the failure off.
            The built becomes "{built} \{ __auto_type cf_el = {element-c}; {map-c}_put(cf_set, cf_el, cf_el); \}".
        Done.
        Return "{built} cf_set; \})".
    Done.

    /// `Insert <value> into <set>.` — put as its own key, so a second insert changes nothing.
    Bind void or failure to emit-set-insert unto emitter, given (the node statement, the text set-kind):
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (set-kind)).
        Define value-c as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast set-element on (set-kind)) or pass the failure off.
        Define set-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        // The set first, then the value, as the interpreter works them out.
        Define sides as a series of text with (set-c, value-c).
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (a series of node with (cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast field-of on (statement, 1)), sides).
        Cast one's line on ("\{ {prefix}__auto_type cf_el = {item 2 of sides}; {map-c}_put({item 1 of sides}, cf_el, cf_el); \}").
    Done.

    /// `For each <name> in <set>, repeat:` — over the elements there when it began, in the order
    /// they went in.
    Bind void or failure to emit-set-for-each unto emitter, given (the node statement, the text set-kind):
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define name as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the name becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define over as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define element as cast set-element on (set-kind).
        Define map-c as cast map-c-name on (cast set-storage on (set-kind)).
        Define element-c as cast c-type on (element).
        Define label as "The set".
        If over's kind is "VariableReference", the label becomes "'{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (over, 1))}'".
        Define set-value as cast one's c-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("{map-c}* cf_each = {set-value};").
        Cast one's line on ("int cf_each_n = cf_each->len;").
        Cast one's line on ("{element-c}* cf_vals = ({element-c}*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)(cf_each_n + 1) * sizeof({element-c}));").
        Cast one's line on ("if (cf_each_n > 0) memcpy(cf_vals, cf_each->vals, (size_t)cf_each_n * sizeof({element-c}));").
        Cast one's line on ("for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_each_n; cf_i++) \{").
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes element.
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes element.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
        Cast one's line on ("if (cf_each->len != cf_each_n) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(\"{label} was modified during a for-each loop on line {(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word} — collect into a separate series, or use a While loop if you need to change it while looping.\"));").
        Cast one's line on ("{element-c} {cast c-name on (name)} = cf_vals[cf_i];").
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
        Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.
Done.
